WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.699
Applying Purdue begins with reality, not a blank diagram.

00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:10.293
Inventory assets, document their operational functions, and map actual communication paths.

00:00:10.293 --> 00:00:15.440
Then assign levels where the model clarifies responsibility and trust.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:24.167
If a system performs several functions or crosses levels, record that complexity rather than forcing a misleading label.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:27.524
Use the model to design segmentation.

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:35.803
Group systems with compatible functions and consequences, place controls at meaningful boundaries, and permit only required flows.

00:00:35.803 --> 00:00:40.950
Remote access should enter through managed services, not bypass levels.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:48.782
Administrative paths deserve the same scrutiny as production data because they can change configurations and logic.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.691
Purdue also guides monitoring placement.

00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:55.495
Enterprise boundaries reveal attempted movement toward OT.

00:00:55.495 --> 00:00:59.747
The industrial DMZ provides visibility into cross-environment exchange.

00:00:59.747 --> 00:01:08.026
Site and control-area monitoring can identify new devices, unexpected protocols, engineering activity, and changes in normal communication.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:13.173
Monitoring choices must account for sensitive devices and operational traffic.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:18.767
During incident-response planning, use levels to identify containment options and dependencies.

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:26.599
Blocking a boundary may protect lower levels, but it may also interrupt identity, reporting, or support.

00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:35.326
Plans should distinguish which functions can continue locally, what visibility remains, and who can authorize isolation or shutdown.

00:01:35.326 --> 00:01:42.263
Modern cloud, industrial Internet of Things, mobile, and vendor services challenge a simple hierarchy.

00:01:42.263 --> 00:01:46.067
Some devices communicate directly with cloud platforms.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.976
Remote operations may span sites.

00:01:48.976 --> 00:01:52.333
Software-defined infrastructure can shift functions dynamically.

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:59.270
Extend the analysis with data-flow diagrams, identity architecture, trust boundaries, and environment-specific threat modeling.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.074
The model's value lies in disciplined reasoning.

00:02:03.074 --> 00:02:10.458
It supports segmentation, access control, monitoring, inventory, and response, but it does not replace them.

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:16.052
Validate every conclusion against the actual process, architecture, and operating constraints.
